        "\n",
        "**Reflection:** Which of the three linked views above is playing the role of \"context\" and which is\n",
        "playing \"focus,\" in the sense of the Focus-Context Problem (Slide 18)? Is that the same distinction as\n",
        "brushing, or a different but related idea? Explain briefly.\n",
        "\n",
        "_Your answer:_\n",
        "The overview bar chart (all stores, muted gray except the selection) plays the role of *context* — it keeps the other stores visible so the manager doesn't lose the bigger picture — while the category breakdown and monthly trend charts, both filtered to just the selected store, play the role of *focus*, showing detail for the one thing being investigated. This is related to brushing but not identical: brushing is the *mechanism* (selecting a value links/highlights it across views), while focus+context is the *design goal* that mechanism serves here — detail on the selected item without losing the overview.\n"
      ]
